{
  "summary": "Owen's rescue of his coworkers reveals that his single Slot can retain multiple skills. Seeking water draws him into the damaged cliff orchards, where earned access, imperfect technique and competing household needs turn his appetite for extraordinary movement into a commitment to shared routes.",
  "rationale": "Each chapter follows a connected practical undertaking whose consequences create the next pursuit. Owen's retained combinations accelerate demonstrated advancement without replacing cultivation knowledge, specialist strength or consent. The orchard's inhabitants become partners through work before their boundary dispute becomes Owen's responsibility to navigate.",
  "expected_outcome": "The supermarket and nursery retain a working water diversion and a traversable evacuation connection. Owen reaches Slot Rank 6 with Cling, Air Step and Threadline intact, establishes reciprocal relationships and wants to earn access to Load Share. Blight, the wider apocalypse, the System's purpose and his exceptional capacity remain unresolved.",
  "chapters": [
    {
      "chapter": 1,
      "intent": "Carry Owen from an interrupted night shift through a rescue requiring retained skills, then let survival produce an immediate desire to explore the inhabited heights.",
      "adaptation": "No adaptation to the proposed coverage was needed. Brief practice remains inside the blocked rescue rather than becoming a separate training episode; the aftermath has its own scene.",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "ordinal": 1,
          "brief": {
            "situation": "Owen is facing supermarket shelves while checking an indoor climbing route on his phone and trying to avoid Leanne's attention. Dev is cleaning near the rear loading corridor when unfamiliar roots begin breaking through the building.",
            "pursuit": "Find a way out with his coworkers as the ordinary shift becomes an evacuation.",
            "changes": [
              "The arrival interrupts active screens and human vision with EVERY PERSON HAS RECEIVED ONE SLOT. CHOOSE WHAT YOU WILL BE ABLE TO DO. Root growth splits the rear corridor while the frontage remains reachable from the main shop.",
              "Owen's sheet reads OWEN PRICE; SLOT COUNT: 1; SLOT CAPACITY: UNLIMITED; INSTALLED SKILLS: NONE; SLOT RANK: 1. Comparing it with Leanne's SLOT CAPACITY: 1 establishes a discrepancy, not yet proof that he can use it.",
              "Owen hears Dev beyond the broken floor and abandons the straightforward exit. A surviving wall offers a possible traverse, but his ordinary climbing ability cannot keep him attached to its smooth surface."
            ],
            "future_dependencies": [
              "Owen's capacity must remain unproven until he retains and uses another skill during the rescue.",
              "The shop frontage and substantial stock must survive so people can later make the intact area a refuge."
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "ordinal": 2,
          "brief": {
            "situation": "Dev is stranded beyond the loading-corridor break. Owen can speak to Leanne from the safe side and study the wall, but the starter choice is the only immediately available source of magic.",
            "pursuit": "Choose the permission that will let him reach Dev before the damaged corridor shifts further.",
            "changes": [
              "Owen chooses Cling over Anchor's stability and Kindle's ability to make fire because adhesion answers the present crossing. The choice gives him no rank increase and leaves him without either alternative skill.",
              "He works across the wall using controlled contact and deliberate foot placement. Poor leverage hurts his wrist, forcing him to adjust rather than rely on magical strength; reaching Dev through this first demanding use changes his sheet to SLOT RANK: 2.",
              "Leanne selects Anchor to brace the rescue from the safe side. Owen checks Dev's injured leg and obtains a usable rope from nearby maintenance equipment, but a section of the return wall breaks away before he can bring it back."
            ],
            "future_dependencies": [
              "Cling must continue to require physical positioning, attention and endurance despite increased rank.",
              "The rope needs to cross the new gap before coworkers can establish a route suitable for Dev."
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "ordinal": 3,
          "brief": {
            "situation": "Owen and Dev occupy the remaining loading platform with the rope. A root beside them carries a translucent seed inside a ceramic sleeve; the missing wall now prevents a continuous Cling traverse.",
            "pursuit": "Carry the rescue line across the gap without abandoning the adhesion needed to catch the far wall.",
            "changes": [
              "Touching the intact seed identifies Air Step as a brief foothold on empty air. Owen commits because the gap requires a push where no foothold remains; the source is consumed and his sheet lists both Cling and Air Step without changing rank.",
              "His first weight transfer wastes the foothold while he remains within reach of the platform. With Dev temporarily secure, he makes a recoverable adjustment at the edge, catches his breath and attempts the crossing rather than pausing for unrelated practice.",
              "Owen releases from a Cling hold, pushes from the brief air foothold and catches the far wall with Cling while carrying the rope. Both permissions remain available during the same action, proving his exception and earning SLOT RANK: 3 through a genuinely new combination.",
              "Leanne anchors herself through a secure connection to the safe end while Owen ties the line to surviving structure. Coworkers can now support Dev's crossing instead of requiring him to reproduce Owen's movement."
            ],
            "future_dependencies": [
              "Air Step must require recovery of breath before reuse and must not become flight.",
              "The consumed seed's cultivated-looking sleeve must remain a clue to ownership, not proof that orchard sources are ownerless."
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "ordinal": 4,
          "brief": {
            "situation": "The rescue line is secured, but Dev still needs assistance and Owen's arms are trembling. The public frontage leads outside while unfamiliar terraces rise above the broken roof.",
            "pursuit": "Finish getting his coworkers clear and determine what survival has left them able to do.",
            "changes": [
              "Owen helps staff move Dev across with the fixed rope and Leanne's anchored support, then withdraws through the intact shop to the frontage. Leanne's demanding first Anchor use earns visible advancement of her own.",
              "With immediate danger behind them, Owen accepts help for his wrist instead of concealing the strain to preserve the impression of effortless competence. Leanne credits the rescue but insists that his next departure have a return plan.",
              "From outside, Owen sees pruned terraces, low handrails and moving lights above the roof. The fear of the crossing gives way to pleasure in what his combined skills made possible; he chooses the inhabited-looking orchard as the next place to seek help, food and another skill."
            ],
            "future_dependencies": [
              "Owen's enthusiasm for the heights must coexist with continuing fatigue and responsibility to the people below.",
              "The orchard's visible habitation must inform his approach before he understands whose territory it is."
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
