    {
      "chapter": 6,
      "intent": "Use the storm to test the connected works and relationships, resolve local water and evacuation access through complementary strengths, and leave Owen with an earned next pursuit.",
      "adaptation": "No adaptation to the proposed coverage was needed. Preparation, difficult execution and actual passage occupy separate scenes so the resolution is experienced rather than announced. Owen does not acquire Load Share or resolve the larger boundary quarrel.",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "ordinal": 21,
          "brief": {
            "situation": "Protective work at the boundary is incomplete when heavy rain begins feeding runoff through the damaged channel network. Owen can trace the threatened flow toward the nursery feeder and the supermarket's broken rear.",
            "pursuit": "Get the separated groups working on the same immediate problem before rising water cuts their communication.",
            "changes": [
              "Owen travels the known route to carry warnings and the cultivator's marked diversion plan. He uses rests between Air Steps and does not waste time on an unfamiliar shortcut, arriving tired but able to describe the structures at risk.",
