        {
          "ordinal": 7,
          "brief": {
            "situation": "The maintenance path runs among warm channels, pruned branches and ceramic graft sleeves. Owen can move ahead more easily than Leanne, but doing so would leave her without knowledge of his route.",
            "pursuit": "Find whoever maintains the gate while preserving a way back for both scouts.",
            "changes": [
              "Owen chooses to mark stable turns and wait at difficult sections instead of racing toward promising grafts. The delay lets him notice sleeping hollows and recently handled tools, evidence of ordinary lives interrupted by the terrain break.",
              "He hears movement near a damaged side channel and approaches without taking a patterned seed within reach. A small, furred, many-limbed person retreats with a tool raised.",
              "Owen lowers his rope and backs away from the tools, allowing the frightened stranger to remain nearby rather than turning the encounter into a chase."
            ],
            "future_dependencies": [
              "The stranger is Serri, whose caution concerns damaged home and missing family rather than a test arranged for Owen.",
              "Neither side may gain conversational translation from the System."
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "ordinal": 8,
          "brief": {
            "situation": "Owen and Leanne face Serri across the broken side channel. Speech fails, and Serri repeatedly searches beyond them toward a path severed by the supermarket's arrival.",
            "pursuit": "Show that they are looking for water rather than attacking, and understand enough of Serri's concern to avoid worsening it.",
            "changes": [
              "Using an empty container, visible tools and gestures toward the break, Owen establishes a tentative connection between their water need and Serri's interrupted maintenance. Serri points to a personal family token and calls toward the severed path, suggesting someone is missing.",
              "Serri shows Owen a braced section that would spill onto inhabited hollows if the gate were simply reopened. Owen understands why his proposed shortcut could harm people he had not seen.",
              "Owen chooses to return with repair materials and help search the damaged route. His objective shifts from finding useful supplies to approaching someone whose home has also been broken; Serri permits observation but grants no water or seed rights."
            ],
            "future_dependencies": [
              "Reciprocal access must remain unsettled until the work and agreement in scene 12.",
              "Serri's missing relative must have an independent reason for being beyond the damaged route."
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "chapter": 3,
      "intent": "Develop limited communication through channel work, acquire Threadline through an accountable exchange and turn tentative contact into an enacted water-sharing relationship.",
      "adaptation": "The water agreement is completed in scene 12 rather than before the skill offer, preserving the specified contact payoff. Serri offers Threadline during the repair as an advance for nursery access; installation and imperfect use therefore have room before the agreement lands.",
      "scenes": [
        {
          "ordinal": 9,
          "brief": {
            "situation": "Owen returns with Leanne, containers and ordinary repair materials salvaged from the shop. Serri has remained by the diversion because the damaged channel still threatens both hollows and nursery irrigation.",
            "pursuit": "Agree on a small repair they can understand through demonstration without pretending to understand the whole orchard.",
            "changes": [
              "Owen sets down the materials and lets Serri demonstrate the intended flow in a shallow channel model. He initially points toward the shop too soon; Serri blocks that outlet until he acknowledges the nursery branch.",
              "They establish practical signals for stop, hold and release by testing unloaded pieces. Owen accepts Serri's authority over the gate while retaining responsibility for whether the human supports are sound.",
