        {
          "ordinal": 13,
          "brief": {
            "situation": "Owen, Leanne and Serri set out with water and nursery supplies. Serri's relative is waiting beyond damaged ledges; Owen has practised keeping short Threadlines steady during necessary preparation but has not built a moving route with them.",
            "pursuit": "Reach the stranded nursery without damaging the living structures Serri identifies along the way.",
            "changes": [
              "Serri redirects Owen from apparently convenient roots that support vulnerable grafts and points out sound endpoint surfaces. He gives up the direct climb in order to keep the route from destroying what they came to preserve.",
              "Owen touches secure endpoints reached through Cling and a breath-recovered Air Step, then maintains a temporary supply guide while returning across uneven surfaces. Sustaining Threadline through this new movement combination demands deliberate attention and earns SLOT RANK: 5.",
